###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The tables give 'average errors' defined through absolute differences; they are encoded as MAE. The stress error is defined as sigma_MTP - sigma_DFT for the diagonal component, without an absolute value in the caption; it is encoded as MAE on that reading.
# - The MTP level (size of the basis) and the software version were not found in the text read; only the 6.2 A cutoff is encoded. The 700 K energy error (2.56 meV/atom) is much larger than at 300 and 500 K, as printed.
# - Lattice thermal conductivities from the Boltzmann transport equation and Green-Kubo MD (Table II last column, Fig. 6) and phonon dispersions are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
